    <div class="container">
      <div id="services">
        <h1>Our services</h1>
        <hr />
        <div class="registration-wrapper">
          <section class="registration-block">
            <header class="reg-header">
              <h2>Registration Requirements</h2>
              <p class="subtitle">
                Guidelines for registration and licensing under the Royal
                Council of Veterinary Doctors (RCVD).
              </p>
            </header>

            <div class="card">
              <h3>Required Documents</h3>
              <ul class="styled-list">
                <li>Letter addressed to the Chairperson of RCVD</li>
                <li>Notified diploma/degree</li>
                <li>Copy of ID card</li>
                <li>Photo passport</li>
                <li>
                  Bank slip of <strong>30,000 RWF</strong> deposited at RCVD
                  account <strong>BK 0004000653033-35</strong>
                </li>
                <li>Filled Application Form</li>
              </ul>
              <p>
                <strong>Registration fees for foreigners:</strong>
                <span class="highlight">50,000 RWF</span>
              </p>
              <p class="note">
                <strong>Attention:</strong> Fresh graduates registered within
                the first 6 months are waived for <strong>50%</strong> of
                registration fees.
              </p>
            </div>

            <h2 id="license">License</h2>
            <div class="card">
              <h3>Requirements</h3>
              <ul class="styled-list">
                <li>
                  License application letter addressed to the Chairperson
                  specifying 1–3 non-conflicting veterinary services and
                  intended practice zone (district, sector).
                </li>
                <li>
                  Copy of previous license (for practitioners already licensed).
                </li>
                <li>
                  Business registration certificate or recommendation letter
                  from the sector level.
                </li>
                <li>Color passport photo.</li>
                <li>
                  Evidence of annual licensing fee payment (Bank of Kigali –
                  RCVD 00040-00653033-35).
                </li>
                <li>
                  Proof of participation in CPD activities — minimum 20 credit
                  points per year (professionals) or 14 points
                  (paraprofessionals).
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
              <h3>Available Fields of Practice</h3>
              <div class="columns">
                <ul>
                  <li>
                    Curative and preventive veterinary medicine (veterinary
                    clinic)
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Veterinary pharmacy practice and livestock equipment use
                  </li>
                  <li>Animal feeds and feeding</li>
                  <li>Bovine artificial insemination</li>
                  <li>Swine artificial insemination</li>
                  <li>Hygiene and quality of animal products</li>
                </ul>
                <ul>
                  <li>Wild animal medicine</li>
                  <li>Animal resources extension &amp; advisory services</li>
                  <li>Education</li>
                  <li>Research</li>
                  <li>Veterinary consultancy</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
              <h3>Licensing Fees</h3>
              <table class="fees-table">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Category</th>
                    <th>Fee (RWF)</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td>
                      Veterinary Doctors / Animal Scientists / Veterinary
                      Technologists
                    </td>
                    <td>30,000</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>Veterinary Paraprofessionals A1</td>
                    <td>20,000</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>Veterinary Paraprofessionals A2</td>
                    <td>15,000</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>Provisional License</td>
                    <td>Free</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>Foreigners (Professionals)</td>
                    <td>100,000</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>Foreigners (Paraprofessionals)</td>
                    <td>50,000</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
              <h3>Provisional License Requirements</h3>
              <ul class="styled-list">
                <li>Letter addressed to the Chairperson</li>
                <li>Copy of registration certificate</li>
                <li>Copy of ID</li>
                <li>Photo passport</li>
                <li>
                  Declaration form completed by a Supervisor (5+ years
                  experience)
                </li>
                <li>Copy of Supervisor’s license</li>
              </ul>
              <p class="note">
                Free of charge if requested during the internship period (first
                6–12 months). Interns must secure placement before applying.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
              <h3>Other Services</h3>
              <ul class="styled-list">
                <li>Registration of Companies under sanitary mandate</li>
                <li>
                  Recommendation Letters for Veterinary Practitioners and
                  Companies
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
              <h3>Other Activities</h3>
              <ul class="styled-list">
                <li>Establish and enforce the veterinary code of ethics</li>
                <li>
                  Promote self-respect, integrity, and professional secrecy
                </li>
                <li>
                  Inspect veterinary practitioners, companies, and premises for
                  compliance
                </li>
                <li>
                  Conduct annual veterinary medicine and animal health school
                  audits
                </li>
                <li>
                  Enhance capacity building for professionals and
                  paraprofessionals
                </li>
                <li>Manage disciplinary actions</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>

